Title: Mary Had a Little Lamb
Credit: Written by
Author: Traditional
Source: Adapted from the nursery rhyme
Draft date: 8/3/2026
Notes: Medium = stylized children's picture-book illustration.

FADE IN:

EXT. COUNTRY LANE - DAY

A sunlit dirt path winds past green meadows. MARY, a gentle girl of about eight with brown hair in neat ribbons, a blue dress and white pinafore, walks with a small basket. At her side trots a small LAMB, its fleece pure white as snow.

NARRATOR
Mary had a little lamb,
Its fleece was white as snow.

EXT. SCHOOLYARD - DAY

A simple wooden schoolhouse stands in a bright yard. Children play near the steps. Mary approaches the door. The small white lamb trots right behind her.

NARRATOR
He followed her to school one day,
That was against the rule.

INT. SCHOOLROOM - DAY

A TEACHER waits at the front. Mary takes a seat. The white lamb stands in the aisle.

CHILDREN
What makes the lamb love Mary so?

TEACHER
Oh, Mary loves the lamb, you know.

FADE OUT.

THE END
